{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.bluffton.edu/employment/adj-edu-math.aspx": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor in Education: K-5 Mathematics Methods",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor in Education: K-5 Mathematics Methods skip to main content Bluffton University Menu Close Menu Admission & aid Admission & Aid Apply Visit Financial Aid Accepted Students Adult and Graduate Students Transfer Students International Students Undergraduate academics Academics Programs of Study Student Success Center for Career and Vocation Cross-Cultural Experiences Bluffton Blueprint Academic Honors Academic Resources Adult & graduate academics Master of Business Administration Master of Arts in Education Master of Social Work Master of Nutrition and Dietetics Student life Student Life Student Engagement Intramurals Residence Life Spiritual Life Multicultural Affairs Health & Wellness Student Handbook About About Bluffton Facts & Figures Visit & Directions Campus Facilities News & Events We Are Beavers All Directory Employment Athletics Blufftonbeavers.com Athletics Hall of Fame Athletic Enews Signup We Remember 3/2/2007 Request info Visit Apply Give Search Search Close Search Info For: Current students Parents & families Faculty & staff Alumni & friends my.Bluffton Moodle News & Events Home Employment Adjunct Instructor in Education: K-5 Mathematics Methods The following statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of\n                           work being performed. They are not intended to be construed as an exhaustive list\n                           of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required of personnel so classified. POSITION SUMMARY: Bluffton University Department of Education is seeking an experienced and student-centered\n                        Adjunct Faculty member to teach K–5 Mathematics Methods courses within the Educator\n                        Preparation Program. The successful candidate will bring expertise in elementary mathematics\n                        instruction and a demonstrated commitment to preparing future educators to teach mathematics\n                        effectively, confidently, and equitably. The instructor will provide preservice teachers with research-based instructional\n                        strategies, practical classroom applications, and opportunities to develop the knowledge\n                        and skills necessary to plan, implement, assess, and differentiate high-quality mathematics\n                        instruction for students in grades K–5. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Teach an undergraduate K–5 Mathematics Methods course in accordance with college and\n                           program standards. Prepare and deliver engaging, evidence-based instruction focused on effective mathematics\n                           teaching practices for elementary learners. Model instructional strategies and pedagogical approaches appropriate for students\n                           in grades K–5. Guide teacher candidates in developing mathematics lesson plans, learning activities,\n                           assessments, and instructional sequences aligned with state and national mathematics\n                           standards. Support teacher candidates in understanding mathematical concepts, student mathematical\n                           thinking, and common misconceptions. Address differentiated instruction and strategies for meeting the needs of diverse\n                           learners, including students with varying levels of mathematical readiness. Integrate problem solving, mathematical reasoning, discourse, representation, fluency,\n                           and conceptual understanding into methods instruction. Incorporate appropriate technology, manipulatives, and other instructional resources\n                           to support elementary mathematics learning. Provide timely, constructive feedback on assignments, lesson plans, and other course-related\n                           work. Maintain accurate course records and comply with college policies, procedures, and\n                           academic expectations. Collaborate with education faculty and contribute to the continued development of\n                           the teacher preparation program as appropriate. QUALIFICATIONS: Minimum: Master’s degree in Education or a closely related field from an accredited institution. Five or more years of successful teaching experience in mathematics at the K–5 level. Demonstrated knowledge of effective elementary mathematics pedagogy and instructional\n                           practices. Strong understanding of elementary mathematics content and the developmental needs\n                           of K–5 learners. Experience designing and implementing standards-aligned mathematics instruction and\n                           assessment. Excellent communication, organization, and interpersonal skills Preferred: Experience teaching mathematics methods or supervising preservice teachers in a teacher\n                           preparation program. Experience working with adult learners, teacher candidates, or professional development\n                           programs. Knowledge of current research and best practices in elementary mathematics education. Familiarity with state and national mathematics standards, including the Common Core\n                           State Standards for Mathematics. Experience integrating educational technology into mathematics instruction. Current or prior elementary teaching licensure/certification. Physical Demands/Work Environment: The position includes approximately twelve hours of in-person classes and labs per\n                           week plus attendance at meetings and other events on campus each week. Lab work includes\n                           some physical labor demands. Some occasional travel off campus may be needed for conferences\n                           and/or off campus meetings. Employment decisions are based on merit and university needs, and not on race, color,\n                     national origin, ancestry, sex, age, disability, marital status, sexual orientation,\n                     gender identity or any other status protected by law. As a religious institution,\n                     Bluffton University expressly reserves its rights to appoint faculty and staff who\n                     share a commitment to the Christian faith which is consistent with the Mennonite/Anabaptist\n                     beliefs of the university’s founding and supporting church. EOE. DEADLINE : Consideration of applications will begin immediately and continue until this position\n                           is filled. APPLICATION MATERIALS: Applications are considered complete when the following materials are received at\n                        the office indicated below: Letter of interest Resume Supplemental Application Completed Bluffton employment application Send application materials to: Human resources Bluffton University 1 University Drive Bluffton, OH 45817-2104 hr@bluffton.edu Posted 09/11/26 Bluffton University Contact us Directions Campus map Employment Media LinkedIn Facebook Instagram YouTube All Rights reserved © 2026| 1 University Drive, Bluffton, Ohio 45817 419-358-3000 Accreditation information Consumer information Privacy policy Top ©"
    },
    "https://www.bluffton.edu/employment/adj-english.aspx": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor in English",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor in English skip to main content Bluffton University Menu Close Menu Admission & aid Admission & Aid Apply Visit Financial Aid Accepted Students Adult and Graduate Students Transfer Students International Students Undergraduate academics Academics Programs of Study Student Success Center for Career and Vocation Cross-Cultural Experiences Bluffton Blueprint Academic Honors Academic Resources Adult & graduate academics Master of Business Administration Master of Arts in Education Master of Social Work Master of Nutrition and Dietetics Student life Student Life Student Engagement Intramurals Residence Life Spiritual Life Multicultural Affairs Health & Wellness Student Handbook About About Bluffton Facts & Figures Visit & Directions Campus Facilities News & Events We Are Beavers All Directory Employment Athletics Blufftonbeavers.com Athletics Hall of Fame Athletic Enews Signup We Remember 3/2/2007 Request info Visit Apply Give Search Search Close Search Info For: Current students Parents & families Faculty & staff Alumni & friends my.Bluffton Moodle News & Events Home Employment Adjunct Instructor in English The following statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of\n                           work being performed. They are not intended to be construed as an exhaustive list\n                           of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required of personnel so classified. POSITION SUMMARY: The Department of Humanities seeks qualified adjunct faculty to teach undergraduate\n                           courses in English composition, American literature, British literature, and creative\n                           writing. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Teach assigned courses in English composition and literature as assigned. Design and deliver course instruction aligned with program outcomes, accreditation\n                              standards, and institutional policies. Develop syllabi, learning activities, assessments, and instructional materials consistent\n                              with approved course descriptions. Evaluate and provide timely, constructive feedback on student work. Maintain regular communication with students and hold virtual or in-person office\n                              hours as required. Use the institution’s learning management system (LMS) to manage course content, grading,\n                              and communication. Uphold academic integrity, accessibility standards, and inclusive teaching practices. Participate in required training, orientation, and assessment activities related to\n                              adjunct teaching. QUALIFICATIONS: Minimum: Earned Master’s degree in English or related field. Experience in teaching English courses at the collegiate level. Preferred: Ph.D. in English or related field. Strong written and oral communication skills. Physical Demands/Work Environment: Primarily a sedentary position with online or hybrid teaching. Employment decisions are based on merit and university needs, and not on race, color,\n                     national origin, ancestry, sex, age, disability, marital status, sexual orientation,\n                     gender identity or any other status protected by law. As a religious institution,\n                     Bluffton University expressly reserves its rights to appoint faculty and staff who\n                     share a commitment to the Christian faith which is consistent with the Mennonite/Anabaptist\n                     beliefs of the university’s founding and supporting church. EOE. DEADLINE : Consideration of applications will begin immediately and continue until this position\n                           is filled. APPLICATION MATERIALS: Applications are considered complete when the following materials are received at\n                        the office indicated below: Letter of interest Resume Supplemental Application Completed Bluffton employment application Send application materials to: Human resources Bluffton University 1 University Drive Bluffton, OH 45817-2104 hr@bluffton.edu Posted 08/11/26 Bluffton University Contact us Directions Campus map Employment Media LinkedIn Facebook Instagram YouTube All Rights reserved © 2026| 1 University Drive, Bluffton, Ohio 45817 419-358-3000 Accreditation information Consumer information Privacy policy Top ©"
    },
    "https://www.bluffton.edu/employment/stf-academicengagement.aspx": {
      "title": "Academic Engagement Specialist",
      "description": "Academic Engagement Specialist - for Musselman Library skip to main content Bluffton University Menu Close Menu Admission & aid Admission & Aid Apply Visit Financial Aid Accepted Students Adult and Graduate Students Transfer Students International Students Undergraduate academics Academics Programs of Study Student Success Center for Career and Vocation Cross-Cultural Experiences Bluffton Blueprint Academic Honors Academic Resources Adult & graduate academics Master of Business Administration Master of Arts in Education Master of Social Work Master of Nutrition and Dietetics Student life Student Life Student Engagement Intramurals Residence Life Spiritual Life Multicultural Affairs Health & Wellness Student Handbook About About Bluffton Facts & Figures Visit & Directions Campus Facilities News & Events We Are Beavers All Directory Employment Athletics Blufftonbeavers.com Athletics Hall of Fame Athletic Enews Signup We Remember 3/2/2007 Request info Visit Apply Give Search Search Close Search Info For: Current students Parents & families Faculty & staff Alumni & friends my.Bluffton Moodle News & Events Home Employment Academic Engagement Specialist - for Musselman Library The following statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of\n                           work being performed. They are not intended to be construed as an exhaustive list\n                           of all responsibilities, duties and skills required of personnel so classified. POSITION SUMMARY: The Academic Engagement Specialist collaborates with faculty, students, and campus\n                           partners to strengthen engagement with library resources and services. The Specialist\n                           develops and delivers instructional programming, creates learning resources, supports\n                           student and faculty research, and promotes the effective use of information and emerging\n                           technologies in teaching and learning. The Specialist reports to the library director. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: INSTRUCTION AND CURRICULUM INTEGRATION Design and facilitate instruction that helps students find, evaluate, and use information\n                           effectively. Partner with faculty to incorporate research skills, information evaluation, and emerging\n                           technologies into courses and assignments. RESEARCH SUPPORT AND LEARNING RESOURCES Provide research assistance to students and faculty through in‑person and virtual\n                           consultations and connect users with appropriate resources and services. Design and develop learning resources (guides, videos, tutorials) to support information\n                           discovery and research. OUTREACH, ENGAGEMENT AND LIBRARY PROGRAMMING Plan, implement, and sustain engagement initiatives that strengthen library connections\n                           with the campus community. Collaborate with library colleagues and campus partners to advance events, services,\n                           and initiatives that align with library mission and goals. Additional Responsibilities: Support library operations as needed and where expertise aligns (e.g circulation desk\n                           coverage, assistance with collection review, offering input on potential acquisitions). Pursue professional development in areas of information literacy, instructional design,\n                           and student success. Qualifications: Minimum: Bachelor’s degree Experience teaching, presenting, training, tutoring, academic coaching, or facilitating\n                           learning experiences for audiences of high school and older Experience with library research Preferred: Master’s degree in a relevant field Experience in higher education Experience in a library, learning center, or similar academic support environment Interest in academic librarianship and/or instructional design Skills/Abilities: Ability to learn and use new software and technology systems Familiarity with online research tools and learning technologies Experience creating instructional or multimedia content Comfort learning and evaluating emerging technologies and AI tools Excellent communication, collaboration, and organizational skills Physical Demands/Work Environment: Multi-floor library building with limited elevator access and frequent stairway use Lifting and/or pushing 30+ pounds on a book truck Exposure to dust and other allergens Variable temperatures and humidity Travel across campus and occasional off-campus meetings Employment decisions are based on merit and university needs, and not on race, color,\n                     national origin, ancestry, sex, age, disability, marital status, sexual orientation,\n                     gender identity or any other status protected by law. As a religious institution,\n                     Bluffton University expressly reserves its rights to appoint faculty and staff who\n                     share a commitment to the Christian faith which is consistent with the Mennonite/Anabaptist\n                     beliefs of the university’s founding and supporting church. EOE. COMPENSATION : Commensurate with education and experience. DEADLINE : Review of applications begins immediately and continues until an appointment is made. APPLICATION MATERIALS: Applications are considered complete when the following materials are received at\n                        the office indicated below: Letter of interest Resume Copies of transcripts Completed Bluffton employment application Send application materials to: Human resources Bluffton University 1 University Drive Bluffton, OH 45817-2104 hr@bluffton.edu Posted 08/24/26 Bluffton University Contact us Directions Campus map Employment Media LinkedIn Facebook Instagram YouTube All Rights reserved © 2026| 1 University Drive, Bluffton, Ohio 45817 419-358-3000 Accreditation information Consumer information Privacy policy Top ©"
    },
    "https://www.bluffton.edu/employment/staff-assistant-athletic-trainer.aspx": {
      "title": "Assistant athletic trainer",
      "description": "Assistant athletic trainer skip to main content Bluffton University Menu Close Menu Admission & aid Admission & Aid Apply Visit Financial Aid Accepted Students Adult and Graduate Students Transfer Students International Students Undergraduate academics Academics Programs of Study Student Success Center for Career and Vocation Cross-Cultural Experiences Bluffton Blueprint Academic Honors Academic Resources Adult & graduate academics Master of Business Administration Master of Arts in Education Master of Social Work Master of Nutrition and Dietetics Student life Student Life Student Engagement Intramurals Residence Life Spiritual Life Multicultural Affairs Health & Wellness Student Handbook About About Bluffton Facts & Figures Visit & Directions Campus Facilities News & Events We Are Beavers All Directory Employment Athletics Blufftonbeavers.com Athletics Hall of Fame Athletic Enews Signup We Remember 3/2/2007 Request info Visit Apply Give Search Search Close Search Info For: Current students Parents & families Faculty & staff Alumni & friends my.Bluffton Moodle News & Events Home Employment Home Open Secondary Nav Employment Student employment Application (pdf) Supplementary Application Assistant athletic trainer The following statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of\n                           work being performed. They are not intended to be construed as an exhaustive list\n                           of all responsibilities, duties and skills required of personnel so classified. Full time/10 months, evening and/or weekend duties as required POSITION SUMMARY: Coordinates all athletic related medical issues, and assist with non-athletic medical\n                        issues for the student athletes. Ensures all student athletes have been cleared for\n                        collegiate athletics. Provide medical coverage for practice and contests, and evaluate,\n                        treat and rehabilitate athletic injuries. Assist and inform the Head Athletic Trainer\n                        of issues that may arise with student-athletes. Supervise student workers. ESSENTIAL RESPONSIBILITIES: Day to day function of the athletic training room, practices, and games. Coordinates\n                           the distribution, collection, and storage of athletic training equipment and supplies. Provide injury prevention, treatment, and rehabilitation for student-athletes. Designs and supervises rehabilitation programs. Work closely with assigned head coaches. (Maintains effective working relationships\n                           with coaches, administrative staff, student-athletes, and other staff.) Work closely with physicians. Coordinate doctor visits for assigned student-athletes.\n                           Oversees the transportation of student-athletes to doctor, hospital, etc., when needed. Record keeping of injuries and rehabilitation (Maintains injury reports in an appropriate\n                           time frame for all injuries. Maintains up-to-date health history files, insurance\n                           information and rehabilitation records for all student-athletes.) Actively encourages and supports the physical well-being of student-athletes by working\n                           with the coaches to assure that the student-athletes are physically ready to participate,\n                           which includes looking for signs of eating disorders or the use of illegal and/or\n                           unhealthful drugs and supplements and taking appropriate preventive measures, and\n                           establishing healthy workout and practice schedules Actively participates in athletic department functions and meetings, and in University\n                           committees as assigned. Extensive evening and weekend hours required Supervision: Supervise student employees to include training, planning, assigning and directing\n                                 work, coaching, addressing complaints and resolving problems. Must have a mindset of mentoring employees under supervision. Should be able to lead\n                                 in a way that sets a good example, promotes teamwork, and encourages a positive, efficient\n                                 work environment. OCCASIONAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Assist Head Athletic Trainer in completing insurance claim forms and notify insurance\n                           company of bills for student-athletes and the student body Other tasks as assigned by supervisor. Evening and/or weekend duties as needed (determined by supervisor). Supervision of student workers Assist the head athletic trainer to ensure completion of the Pre-Participation Physical\n                           Exam Form, Insurance Form B, Sickle Cell Form, IMPACT testing, and Drug Testing Waiver\n                           prior to athletic participation QUALIFICATION REQUIREMENTS : The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability\n                        required to satisfactorily perform the essential duties of this job. Education/Certification: Bachelors in Athletic Training, NATABOC Certification; Ohio Athletic Training License\n                           or eligible and current CPR\\First Aid certification for the Professional Rescuer. Experience: Previous Athletic Training experience. Skill/Abilities: Excellent written & verbal communication needed, ability to manage multi-task situations. Diversity & Faith Commitment: Bluffton University expects all employees to show respect in the workplace and not\n                           to base business decisions on race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, age, disability,\n                           marital status, sexual orientation, gender identity or any other status protected\n                           by law. As a religious institution, Bluffton University welcomes its faculty and staff\n                           and encourages respectful consideration of the Christian faith which is consistent\n                           with the Mennonite/Anabaptist beliefs of the university’s founding and supporting\n                           church. PHYSICAL DEMANDS/WORK ENVIRONMENT: The physical demands and/or work environment described here are representative of\n                        those that must be met or will be encountered by the employee while performing the\n                        essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals\n                        with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Must occasionally lift and/or move to up to 40 pounds (water coolers and ice chests) Regularly work in outside weather conditions in fall and spring months. APPLICATION MATERIALS: Applications are considered complete when all of the following materials are received\n                        at the office indicated below: Letter of interest Resume Completed Bluffton employment application Review of applications will begin immediately to fill this position as soon as possible. Send employment application materials to: Human Resources Bluffton University 1 University Drive Bluffton, OH 45817-2104 hr@bluffton.edu Employment decisions are based on merit and university needs, and not on race, color,\n                     national origin, ancestry, sex, age, disability, marital status, sexual orientation,\n                     gender identity or any other status protected by law. As a religious institution,\n                     Bluffton University expressly reserves its rights to appoint faculty and staff who\n                     share a commitment to the Christian faith which is consistent with the Mennonite/Anabaptist\n                     beliefs of the university’s founding and supporting church. EOE. Posted 07/02/25 Bluffton University Contact us Directions Campus map Employment Media LinkedIn Facebook Instagram YouTube All Rights reserved © 2026| 1 University Drive, Bluffton, Ohio 45817 419-358-3000 Accreditation information Consumer information Privacy policy Top ©"
    },
    "https://www.bluffton.edu/employment/stf-bus-driver.aspx": {
      "title": "Bus driver",
      "description": "Bus driver skip to main content Bluffton University Menu Close Menu Admission & aid Admission & Aid Apply Visit Financial Aid Accepted Students Adult and Graduate Students Transfer Students International Students Undergraduate academics Academics Programs of Study Student Success Center for Career and Vocation Cross-Cultural Experiences Bluffton Blueprint Academic Honors Academic Resources Adult & graduate academics Master of Business Administration Master of Arts in Education Master of Social Work Master of Nutrition and Dietetics Student life Student Life Student Engagement Intramurals Residence Life Spiritual Life Multicultural Affairs Health & Wellness Student Handbook About About Bluffton Facts & Figures Visit & Directions Campus Facilities News & Events We Are Beavers All Directory Employment Athletics Blufftonbeavers.com Athletics Hall of Fame Athletic Enews Signup We Remember 3/2/2007 Request info Visit Apply Give Search Search Close Search Info For: Current students Parents & families Faculty & staff Alumni & friends my.Bluffton Moodle News & Events Home Employment Home Open Secondary Nav Employment Student employment Application (pdf) Supplementary Application Bus driver The following statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of\n                           work being performed. They are not intended to be construed as an exhaustive list\n                           of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required of personnel so classified . Part-time, as needed POSITION SUMMARY : Provides bus transportation services for university faculty, staff and students, ensuring\n                        safe and dependable transportation. ESSENTIAL RESPONSIBILITIES: Drive the Bluffton University owned bus, providing safe and efficient transportation\n                           for the university community. Comply with all federal, state, and local regulations related to the operation of\n                           the Bluffton University bus. Follow all requirements found within the Bluffton University Bus Operations Policies\n                           and Procedures manual. Submit complete and accurate hours of service records and driver’s time records. Perform routine vehicle pre-trip and post-trip inspections. Make timely reports of accidents, incidents and unusual occurrences. SECONDARY RESPONSIBILITIES: Assist in transporting the bus for scheduled vehicle maintenance. QUALIFICATION REQUIREMENTS : The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability\n                        required to satisfactorily perform the essential responsibilities of this job. Minimum: Education/Certification: Must be at least 21 years old. Drivers must have a valid Commercial Driver’s License\n                           (CDL) which allows the drivers to operate: A vehicle designed to transport more than\n                           15 passengers, a single vehicle with a gross vehicle weight rating of more than 26,001\n                           pounds, and a vehicle with air brakes. Drivers will need to be registered and pass\n                           a full-query background check with the FMCSA Clearinghouse Portal before employment\n                           is authorized and then pass limited-query checks annually thereafter. Drivers must\n                           pass a DOT physical and be self-certified with the Bureau of Motor Vehicles. Drivers\n                           must submit all items as required by the Department of Transportation and the Driver\n                           Qualifications Checklist. PHYSICAL DEMANDS / WORK ENVIRONMENT : The physical demands and/or work environment described here are representative of\n                        those that must be met or will be encountered by the employee while performing the\n                        essential functions of this job.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable\n                        individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Physical requirements\n                        must be in compliance with all provisions of DOT Regulation. Work environment involves\n                        some exposure to hazards or physical risks, which require following basic safety precautions.\n                        Work may involve moderate exposure to unusual weather elements, such as extreme temperatures,\n                        dirt, dust, fumes, smoke, unpleasant odors and/or loud noises. DEADLINE: Review of applications begins immediately, and continues until position is filled. APPLICATION MATERIALS: Applications are considered complete when the following materials are received at\n                        the office indicated below: Letter of interest Resume Completed Bluffton employment application Send application materials to: hr@bluffton.edu Employment decisions are based on merit and university needs, and not on race, color,\n                     national origin, ancestry, sex, age, disability, marital status, sexual orientation,\n                     gender identity or any other status protected by law. As a religious institution,\n                     Bluffton University expressly reserves its rights to appoint faculty and staff who\n                     share a commitment to the Christian faith which is consistent with the Mennonite/Anabaptist\n                     beliefs of the university’s founding and supporting church. EOE. Posted 06/25/25 Bluffton University Contact us Directions Campus map Employment Media LinkedIn Facebook Instagram YouTube All Rights reserved © 2026| 1 University Drive, Bluffton, Ohio 45817 419-358-3000 Accreditation information Consumer information Privacy policy Top ©"
    },
    "https://www.bluffton.edu/employment/stf-custodian.aspx": {
      "title": "Custodial Services Associate",
      "description": "Custodial Services Associate skip to main content Bluffton University Menu Close Menu Admission & aid Admission & Aid Apply Visit Financial Aid Accepted Students Adult and Graduate Students Transfer Students International Students Undergraduate academics Academics Programs of Study Student Success Center for Career and Vocation Cross-Cultural Experiences Bluffton Blueprint Academic Honors Academic Resources Adult & graduate academics Master of Business Administration Master of Arts in Education Master of Social Work Master of Nutrition and Dietetics Student life Student Life Student Engagement Intramurals Residence Life Spiritual Life Multicultural Affairs Health & Wellness Student Handbook About About Bluffton Facts & Figures Visit & Directions Campus Facilities News & Events We Are Beavers All Directory Employment Athletics Blufftonbeavers.com Athletics Hall of Fame Athletic Enews Signup We Remember 3/2/2007 Request info Visit Apply Give Search Search Close Search Info For: Current students Parents & families Faculty & staff Alumni & friends my.Bluffton Moodle News & Events Home Employment Home Open Secondary Nav Employment Student employment Application (pdf) Supplementary Application Custodial Services Associate The following statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of\n                           work being performed. They are not intended to be construed as an exhaustive list\n                           of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required of personnel so classified . Full time; evening and/or weekend duties as required POSITION SUMMARY : The Custodial Services Associate is responsible for performing hands on custodial\n                        duties for assigned campus areas to ensure the buildings and associated areas are\n                        maintained in a healthy, safe and sanitary condition. The position may include supervision\n                        of student custodians as well. ESSENTIAL RESPONSIBILITIES: Functional Duties: Ensure high levels of cleanliness of all assigned areas. The work is to include but\n                           not limited to: cleaning of floors, ensuring all washrooms are cleaned and sanitized\n                           with supplies replenished. Ensures the removal of all trash, clean and disinfects\n                           all required surfaces in assigned areas. Inventory, order, and restock custodial supplies.\n                           This position will assist throughout the campus with University Events set-up and\n                           tear down as needed. Perform and/or report minor maintenance repairs while assisting\n                           maintenance staff. Assist with all stages and methods of snow removal. Supervision: May supervise student employees to include training, planning, assigning and directing\n                           work, inspecting work, coaching, addressing complaints and resolving problems. Must\n                           have a mindset of mentoring employees under supervision. Should be able to lead in\n                           a way that sets a good example, promotes teamwork and encourages a positive, efficient\n                           work environment. Other: May need to work early morning or late evenings with some weekend duties being required.\n                           Handles all other tasks as assigned. QUALIFICATION REQUIREMENTS : The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill and/or ability\n                        required to satisfactorily perform the essential duties of this job. Minimum: High school diploma or equivalent and a positive work ethic. Preferred: Previous custodial experience and/or training in related field. Knowledge and understanding of institutional cleaning standards and cleaning equipment,\n                           training in cleaning techniques and products. Has shown effective interpersonal skills with proven ability to manage multiple tasks\n                           along with a commitment to service. PHYSICAL DEMANDS / WORK ENVIRONMENT : The physical demands and/or work environment encountered by the employee while performing\n                        the essential responsibilities of this job must be met with or without reasonable\n                        accommodations. Reasonable accommodations will be considered and implemented when\n                        possible to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential responsibilities\n                        of this position. Job function requires standing, sitting and walking significant distance between and\n                        within buildings. Individuals must be able to frequently lift/carry items weighting\n                        up to 30 pounds and seasonally lift items up to 75 pounds, frequently bend, stoop,\n                        and climb stairs and ladders. Must possess sufficient manual dexterity to operate\n                        typical custodial and grounds and maintenance equipment. Deadline Review of applications begins immediately, and continues until position is filled. APPLICATION MATERIALS: Applications are considered complete when the following materials are received at\n                        the office indicated below: Letter of interest Resume Completed Bluffton employment application Send application materials to: hr@bluffton.edu Employment decisions are based on merit and university needs, and not on race, color,\n                     national origin, ancestry, sex, age, disability, marital status, sexual orientation,\n                     gender identity or any other status protected by law. As a religious institution,\n                     Bluffton University expressly reserves its rights to appoint faculty and staff who\n                     share a commitment to the Christian faith which is consistent with the Mennonite/Anabaptist\n                     beliefs of the university’s founding and supporting church. EOE. Posted 06/25/25 Bluffton University Contact us Directions Campus map Employment Media LinkedIn Facebook Instagram YouTube All Rights reserved © 2026| 1 University Drive, Bluffton, Ohio 45817 419-358-3000 Accreditation information Consumer information Privacy policy Top ©"
    },
    "https://www.bluffton.edu/employment/stf-finaid-officer-asstdirector.aspx": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Officer/Asst. Director of Financial Aid",
      "description": "Financial Aid Officer/Asst. Director of Financial Aid skip to main content Bluffton University Menu Close Menu Admission & aid Admission & Aid Apply Visit Financial Aid Accepted Students Adult and Graduate Students Transfer Students International Students Undergraduate academics Academics Programs of Study Student Success Center for Career and Vocation Cross-Cultural Experiences Bluffton Blueprint Academic Honors Academic Resources Adult & graduate academics Master of Business Administration Master of Arts in Education Master of Social Work Master of Nutrition and Dietetics Student life Student Life Student Engagement Intramurals Residence Life Spiritual Life Multicultural Affairs Health & Wellness Student Handbook About About Bluffton Facts & Figures Visit & Directions Campus Facilities News & Events We Are Beavers All Directory Employment Athletics Blufftonbeavers.com Athletics Hall of Fame Athletic Enews Signup We Remember 3/2/2007 Request info Visit Apply Give Search Search Close Search Info For: Current students Parents & families Faculty & staff Alumni & friends my.Bluffton Moodle News & Events Home Employment Financial Aid Officer/Asst. Director of Financial Aid The following statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of\n                           work being performed. They are not intended to be construed as an exhaustive list\n                           of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required of personnel so classified. POSITION SUMMARY: The Financial Aid Officer/Assist. Director of Financial Aid assists the Director of\n                           Financial Aid in administering all aspects of student financial aid at Bluffton University\n                           including all federal, state and institutional grants, scholarships, loans and student\n                           work programs. The Financial Aid Officer/Assist. Director of Financial Aid must maintain\n                           a comprehensive knowledge of federal, state and institutional financial aid programs\n                           and their regulations, policies and procedures. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: FINANCIAL AID OFFERS Package and update awards for all continuing, traditional students after spring registration\n                           and any other new/prospective student as necessary Operate daily FAFSA/ISIR uploads to PowerFAIDS and initial processing of ISIRs for\n                           packaging. Counsel students and families concerning financial aid processes and scholarship information. Packaging and updating financial aid for AGS students (adult programs). Create and maintain student records and filing system. FINANCIAL AID PROGRAM RESPONSIBILITIES Administer Endowed scholarships Administer OFIC scholarships Conduct all verifications of federally selected FAFSA filers and maintain tracking\n                           and corrections for these records. Ensure compliance with federal and institutional\n                           verification policies. Resolve all issues of conflicting information. Complete Verification\n                           of non-federally selected FAFSA filers for all those who file for special circumstances. Counsel students and families concerning financial aid and the financial aid process Assist with or conduct financial aid presentations/workshops Plan, develop, implement and maintain the writing of the financial aid policies and\n                           procedures manual following the outline from NASFAA Oversee record retention rules and procedures for federal compliance Monthly reconciliation of Federal grant/loan programs (Direct loans, Pell, TEACH). Certification and processing of Private Education Loans Certification and processing of Federal Direct Student and Parent Loans. Disbursing aid to student accounts/reconciling financial aid and student accounts. Financial aid revisions/calculations of withdrawn students (institutional and Federal\n                           requirements) Satisfactory Academic Progress (SAP) monitoring and communicating with students. State Grant reporting and reconciliation (OCOG, War Orphans, National Guard, Choose\n                           Ohio First, etc.) Monitor and administer renewal GPA requirements for Bluffton’s scholarship programs. Secondary responsibilities: Assist with institutional research or surveys as needed or assigned. Oversee special projects as assigned. Represent Bluffton University at professional meetings. Serve as acting Director of Financial Aid in the absence of the Director (only for\n                           AD level) Perform any other task as needed or assigned. QUALIFICATIONS: The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability\n                           required to satisfactorily perform the essential duties of this job. Minimum: Education/Certification: Bachelor’s degree, Master’s preferred Experience: 1-2 years’ experience in financial aid or related field for officer level;\n                           at least 2-3 years of experience in financial aid for assistant director level Skills: Knowledge of computer systems: MS Word and Excel, ACCESS, PC network environment,\n                              data base systems/CRMs, integrated software applications; knowledge of federal, state,\n                              institutional financial aid programs, their regulations, policies and procedures;\n                              willingness to attend special training. Special Abilities: Ability to work effectively and positively with students and families on sensitive\n                              financial concerns; ability to demonstrate commitment to exceptional customer service;\n                              demonstrable skills in administration, management and information technology; must\n                              maintain the privacy of sensitive or confidential information at all times; attention\n                              to detail and strong organizational skills; strong interpersonal skills; strong written\n                              and oral communication skills; quick learner and able to work under tight time constraints. Physical Demands/Work Environment: Must possess a valid driver’s license and drive an automobile. Employment decisions are based on merit and university needs, and not on race, color,\n                     national origin, ancestry, sex, age, disability, marital status, sexual orientation,\n                     gender identity or any other status protected by law. As a religious institution,\n                     Bluffton University expressly reserves its rights to appoint faculty and staff who\n                     share a commitment to the Christian faith which is consistent with the Mennonite/Anabaptist\n                     beliefs of the university’s founding and supporting church. EOE. DEADLINE : Consideration of applications will begin immediately and continue until this position\n                           is filled. APPLICATION MATERIALS: Applications are considered complete when the following materials are received at\n                        the office indicated below: Letter of interest Resume Completed Bluffton employment application Send application materials to: Human resources Bluffton University 1 University Drive Bluffton, OH 45817-2104 hr@bluffton.edu Posted 10/13/26 Bluffton University Contact us Directions Campus map Employment Media LinkedIn Facebook Instagram YouTube All Rights reserved © 2026| 1 University Drive, Bluffton, Ohio 45817 419-358-3000 Accreditation information Consumer information Privacy policy Top ©"
    },
    "https://www.bluffton.edu/employment/ga-contentmanagment.aspx": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant for Content Management",
      "description": "Graduate Assistant for Content Management skip to main content Bluffton University Menu Close Menu Admission & aid Admission & Aid Apply Visit Financial Aid Accepted Students Adult and Graduate Students Transfer Students International Students Undergraduate academics Academics Programs of Study Student Success Center for Career and Vocation Cross-Cultural Experiences Bluffton Blueprint Academic Honors Academic Resources Adult & graduate academics Master of Business Administration Master of Arts in Education Master of Social Work Master of Nutrition and Dietetics Student life Student Life Student Engagement Intramurals Residence Life Spiritual Life Multicultural Affairs Health & Wellness Student Handbook About About Bluffton Facts & Figures Visit & Directions Campus Facilities News & Events We Are Beavers All Directory Employment Athletics Blufftonbeavers.com Athletics Hall of Fame Athletic Enews Signup We Remember 3/2/2007 Request info Visit Apply Give Search Search Close Search Info For: Current students Parents & families Faculty & staff Alumni & friends my.Bluffton Moodle News & Events Home Employment Graduate Assistant for Content Management The following statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of\n                           work being performed. They are not intended to be construed as an exhaustive list\n                           of all responsibilities, duties, and skills required of personnel so classified. POSITION SUMMARY: The Graduate Assistant for Content Management will be a self-motivated person with\n                        strong interpersonal and group communication skills, who possesses a passion for written\n                        and digital communication and has strong knowledge the communication, public relations\n                        and journalism fields. This implements annual and multi-year communication strategies\n                        to further the mission and goals of Bluffton University through exemplary communication\n                        practices that build awareness of and promote Bluffton University, engage its constituents\n                        and ultimately builds its reputation as a distinctive university. The Graduate Assistant for Content Management (GA-CM) is responsible to seek out,\n                        research, write, edit, and publish stories that advance the university’s mission and\n                        reputation. The GA-CM typically provides in-person coverage of many campus events\n                        and student and faculty accomplishments. Stories are produced for distribution through\n                        multiple channels including print, web, social media, and regional and Mennonite media.\n                        The GA-CM writes and produces feature stories and donor profiles for print, digital\n                        and video platforms that communicate Bluffton's mission and values. As a member of\n                        the PR staff, the GA-CM assists with planning and coordination of public relations\n                        responsibilities including internal communications, special events, and media relations\n                        as needed. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Content Development Research, plan, write and edit stories that communicate the impact and value of Bluffton\n                           University to internal and external audiences, with a priority on advancement and\n                           admissions strategic objectives, including: Beavers All feature stories, Alumnote\n                           Features, news releases and event coverage, and write and send multiple monthly enewsletters. Collaborate with the PR and admissions directors in developing content and writing\n                           for integrated marketing efforts, e.g. developing message maps and content for campaigns\n                           and the admissions communication flow. Responsible for timely distribution of news stories and photos to Bluffton.edu and\n                           to the media. Responsible for media relations, obtaining and managing campus media coverage. Serve as strategist to write and manage the monthly tactical plan. Assign, manage\n                           and edit story assignments by student and staff writers. Provide proofreading services for all publications in PR office production flow using\n                           AP style. Support campus offices with all writing needs As a member of the public relations creative team, implement and uphold the application\n                           of Bluffton University’s visual identity standards and editorial style guide. Support\n                           campus integration with these standards across all projects. Accountable for achieving\n                           Bluffton’s expected high level of quality on all designed materials. The CM will possess strong writing, verbal communication and editing skills and will\n                           enjoy participating as a member of a creative team and working in a collaborative\n                           environment. Their stories must engage, influence and persuade Bluffton’s constituents.\n                           They will have the organizational skills and ability to balance multiple projects\n                           and must meet production deadlines. Occasional Duties and Responsibilities: Assist in the PR office as needed Other tasks as assigned by supervisor C. Some Saturday commitments and occasional evening/weekend work QUALIFICATIONS: Minimum: Education and/or Experience: Bachelor’s degree or higher. Some prior experience in\n                           graphic design and/or media production. Special Skills: As a frequent representative of Bluffton University to the public\n                           and corporate community, the employee must have high ethical standards and excellent\n                           communication and interpersonal skills. Be highly motivated with strong organizational\n                           skills, technology skills and the ability to manage multiple tasks are vital. Integrity\n                           and honesty in conveying program information and respect for prospective students\n                           are essential. Candidate must be friendly, outgoing, self-motivated, and able to delegate,\n                           and have excellent written and verbal skills. Candidate must also be computer literate\n                           in Microsoft Office, Excel and Word. Must qualify for the Bluffton University Master of Business Administration, Master\n                           of Arts in Education or Master of Social Work program to be considered for the position. Preferred: Education and/or Experience - BA degree. 1 year of prior communication, writing, journalism\n                           and related experience or other college related work. Understanding of the liberal\n                           arts, private college environment within a Christian setting. Bluffton University\n                           graduate. Degree obtained: Master of Business Administration (MBA) Master of Arts in Education (MAEd) OR Master of Social Work (MSW) COMPENSATION : Full tuition waiver with competitive stipend, room and board. DEADLINE : Consideration of applications will begin immediately and continue until this position\n                           is filled. APPLICATION MATERIALS: Applications are considered complete when the following materials are received at\n                        the office indicated below: Letter of interest Resume Completed Bluffton employment application Send application materials to: Human resources Bluffton University 1 University Drive Bluffton, OH 45817-2104 hr@bluffton.edu Employment decisions are based on merit and university needs, and not on race, color,\n                     national origin, ancestry, sex, age, disability, marital status, sexual orientation,\n                     gender identity or any other status protected by law. As a religious institution,\n                     Bluffton University expressly reserves its rights to appoint faculty and staff who\n                     share a commitment to the Christian faith which is consistent with the Mennonite/Anabaptist\n                     beliefs of the university’s founding and supporting church. EOE. Posted 04/13/26 Bluffton University Contact us Directions Campus map Employment Media LinkedIn Facebook Instagram YouTube All Rights reserved © 2026| 1 University Drive, Bluffton, Ohio 45817 419-358-3000 Accreditation information Consumer information Privacy policy Top ©"
    },
    "https://www.bluffton.edu/employment/stf-vp-advancement.aspx": {
      "title": "Vice President of Advancement",
      "description": "Vice President of Advancement skip to main content Bluffton University Menu Close Menu Admission & aid Admission & Aid Apply Visit Financial Aid Accepted Students Adult and Graduate Students Transfer Students International Students Undergraduate academics Academics Programs of Study Student Success Center for Career and Vocation Cross-Cultural Experiences Bluffton Blueprint Academic Honors Academic Resources Adult & graduate academics Master of Business Administration Master of Arts in Education Master of Social Work Master of Nutrition and Dietetics Student life Student Life Student Engagement Intramurals Residence Life Spiritual Life Multicultural Affairs Health & Wellness Student Handbook About About Bluffton Facts & Figures Visit & Directions Campus Facilities News & Events We Are Beavers All Directory Employment Athletics Blufftonbeavers.com Athletics Hall of Fame Athletic Enews Signup We Remember 3/2/2007 Request info Visit Apply Give Search Search Close Search Info For: Current students Parents & families Faculty & staff Alumni & friends my.Bluffton Moodle News & Events Home Employment Vice President of Advancement The following statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of\n                           work being performed. They are not intended to be construed as an exhaustive list\n                           of all responsibilities, duties and skills required of personnel so classified. POSITION SUMMARY: The Vice President for Advancement provides leadership for all fundraising and constituent\n                        engagement activities that support the mission and strategic priorities of Bluffton\n                        University. This position directs a comprehensive advancement program, including annual\n                        giving, major and planned gifts, corporate and foundation relations, and alumni and\n                        parent engagement. The Vice President is responsible for developing and executing strategies that build\n                        philanthropic support and foster lifelong relationships between the university and\n                        its alumni, donors, and community partners. The Vice President serves as a member\n                        of the President’s Cabinet and staff representative to the Advancement Committee of\n                        the Board of Trustees. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: LEADERSHIP Serve as member of the President’s Cabinet. Direct, supervise, and mentor staff in Advancement, Alumni Relations, and Development. Provide leadership and oversight for all fundraising initiatives, including comprehensive\n                           campaigns. Develop and implement strategies to strengthen alumni, donor, and community engagement. Partner with the President and Board of Trustees on cultivation and solicitation of\n                           major and planned gifts. Serve as staff liaison to the Board’s Advancement Committee. Set a tone of professionalism, accountability, and mission commitment within the Advancement\n                           team. FUNDRAISING AND DONOR ENGAGEMENT Design and implement a comprehensive advancement plan that includes annual giving,\n                           major gifts, planned giving, and corporate and foundation support. Establish fundraising goals and track progress toward annual and campaign objectives. Maintain a portfolio of major donors with annual fundraising goals of $1M+ through\n                           relationship management. Travel anticipated to be at least 30% of working schedule. Responsible for meeting annual fundraising goals. Coordinate and support the President’s role in donor cultivation and stewardship. Develop and maintain relationships with alumni, parents, friends, and organizations\n                           to increase philanthropic support. Provide oversight for advancement recognition programs and donor reporting. FINANCIAL OVERSIGHT Ensure appropriate stewardship and reporting of gifts. Oversee policies and procedures for prospect management, donor records, and gift accounting\n                           in coordination with Finance and Advancement Services. ALUMNI AND COMMUNITY RELATIONS Strengthen the university’s alumni engagement strategy, including events, communications,\n                           and volunteer leadership. Partner with alumni to expand mentoring, networking, and career opportunities for\n                           students and graduates. Represent Bluffton University in the community and in professional advancement organizations. BLUFFTON COLLEGE FOUNDATION RELATIONS Serve as the university’s primary Advancement liaison to the Bluffton College Foundation,\n                           fostering a collaborative relationship with Foundation trustees and leadership and\n                           supporting Foundation operations as agreed upon by university administration and the\n                           Foundation’s Board of Trustees. Coordinate university and Foundation advancement objectives and activities to support\n                           effective donor engagement, gift administration, and stewardship. Qualifications: Education/Certification: Bachelor’s degree required; master’s degree in business, higher education, nonprofit\n                           leadership, advancement, or a related field preferred. Evidence of continued professional development in fundraising, advancement, nonprofit\n                           leadership, or higher education. Experience: Significant progressively responsible experience in advancement, development, fundraising,\n                           alumni relations, nonprofit leadership, or a closely related field. Demonstrated success in cultivating, soliciting, and stewarding major gifts and in\n                           building sustained philanthropic relationships. Experience developing and executing comprehensive fundraising strategies, including\n                           annual giving, major and planned gifts, campaigns, and corporate and foundation support. Demonstrated experience leading, supervising, and developing professional staff and\n                           building effective teams. Experience working effectively with senior institutional leaders, governing boards,\n                           volunteers, donors, and other external constituents. Higher education advancement experience preferred. Skills/Abilities: Demonstrated ability to translate institutional mission, strategic priorities, and\n                           financial needs into compelling philanthropic opportunities and a coherent advancement\n                           strategy. Strong relationship-building skills and the ability to establish trust with donors,\n                           alumni, colleagues, trustees, community partners, and other constituents. Ability to serve as a strategic advisor and collaborative partner to the President\n                           while exercising appropriate initiative, judgment, and independent leadership within\n                           the responsibilities of the position. Demonstrated ability to lead complex initiatives collaboratively across organizational\n                           boundaries and to work effectively as a member of a senior leadership team. Strong organizational and management skills, including the ability to establish priorities,\n                           manage multiple initiatives, use data to assess performance, and hold oneself and\n                           others accountable for results. Demonstrated understanding of advancement operations, including prospect management,\n                           gift administration and stewardship, fundraising forecasting and reporting, and the\n                           appropriate handling of restricted and unrestricted philanthropic resources. Excellent written, verbal, interpersonal, and presentation skills, including the ability\n                           to communicate effectively with individuals and groups at all levels of the university\n                           and with external constituents. Demonstrated commitment to ethical fundraising practices, donor intent, confidentiality,\n                           and responsible stewardship. Ability to understand, articulate, and advance Bluffton University’s mission and identity,\n                           including its grounding in the historic peace church tradition and its commitment\n                           to educating students of all backgrounds. Physical Demands/Work Environment: The physical demands and/or work environment encountered by the employee while performing\n                           the essential responsibilities of this job must be met with or without reasonable\n                           accommodations. Reasonable accommodations will be considered and implemented when\n                           possible to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential responsibilities\n                           of this position. Secondary responsibilities may be removed when needed as an accommodation\n                           strategy. Physical Demands: While performing the duties of this position, the employee is regularly required\n                        to sit, talk, and hear. The employee frequently is required to use hands to handle\n                        or operate office equipment, reach with hands and arms, and occasionally stand, walk,\n                        and lift or move up to 20 pounds. The position requires the ability to travel by automobile\n                        and commercial air for donor visits, events, and professional meetings. Extended periods\n                        of computer work and occasional evening and weekend responsibilities are expected. Work Environment: The work environment is primarily a professional office setting on Bluffton University’s\n                        campus, with frequent off-site travel for donor engagement, alumni events, and university\n                        functions. The noise level in the work environment is typically moderate. During travel,\n                        the employee may experience varied work environments including conference facilities,\n                        event venues, airports, and other public or private locations. Employment decisions are based on merit and university needs, and not on race, color,\n                     national origin, ancestry, sex, age, disability, marital status, sexual orientation,\n                     gender identity or any other status protected by law. As a religious institution,\n                     Bluffton University expressly reserves its rights to appoint faculty and staff who\n                     share a commitment to the Christian faith which is consistent with the Mennonite/Anabaptist\n                     beliefs of the university’s founding and supporting church. EOE. DEADLINE : Consideration of applications will begin immediately and continue until this position\n                           is filled. APPLICATION MATERIALS: Applications are considered complete when the following materials are received at\n                        the office indicated below: Letter of interest Resume Completed Bluffton employment application Send application materials to: Human resources Bluffton University 1 University Drive Bluffton, OH 45817-2104 hr@bluffton.edu Posted 10/19/26 Bluffton University Contact us Directions Campus map Employment Media LinkedIn Facebook Instagram YouTube All Rights reserved © 2026| 1 University Drive, Bluffton, Ohio 45817 419-358-3000 Accreditation information Consumer information Privacy policy Top"
    }
  },
